{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form","id":881131,"title":"Why CAN'T Lunars use Martial Arts in animal form?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-03T11:45:18-07:00","id":881131,"title":"Why CAN'T Lunars use Martial Arts in animal form?","content":"I'm pretty sure the devs confirmed Lunars don't get access to MA charms in their animal form, but I'd like to ask why this would be if so. Because it sounds <i>awesome </i>to me! Picture the proud Immaculate Monk, having to spar with a Crane using Crane Style! It sounds like a ton of fun. Would it really be that far out there from Lunars using their regular charms in animal form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:48:19-07:00","id":881137,"title":"","content":"Not sure about that, but probably because martial arts are build upon certain katas and essence flows made for human beings, which cannot really be replicated in form of an animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:50:47-07:00","id":881141,"title":"","content":"A tiger already moves and fights like a tiger.<br /> <br /> Tiger Style is a human pretending to be a tiger.<br /> <br /> A tiger trying to use Tiger Style would need to pretend to be a human pretending to be a tiger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:51:13-07:00","id":881142,"title":"","content":"Because martial arts were designed to be used by people emulating animals. Not by animals themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:00:55-07:00","id":881150,"title":"","content":"They can. Maybe the writers intend to change that, but for the time being there are no restrictions.<br /> <br /> If and when that changes, I expect they'll provide a justification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:12:29-07:00","id":881157,"title":"","content":"a lunar can use martial arts charms while in warform - that's basically an animal form<br /> <br /> the trick is that martial arts charms require human or humanoid form - a lunar in an animal form... simply doesn't have the range of movements required for martial arts. Sure, a few might sort of fit the bill, but overall animals simply do not have the bits for it.<br /> <br /> Maybe an essence 5 custom knack would allow for it - to a certain extent.<br /> <br /> The thing is that it just doesn't make sense for a mouse, or a cat, to punch and kick as hard as a human. A gorrila? Ya I can see that, maybe, and with a knack that increases the range of motion of a human-sized animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:16:46-07:00","id":881160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form#post881131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the devs confirmed Lunars don't get access to MA charms in their animal form, but I'd like to ask why this would be if so. Because it sounds <i>awesome </i>to me! Picture the proud Immaculate Monk, having to spar with a Crane using Crane Style! It sounds like a ton of fun. Would it really be that far out there from Lunars using their regular charms in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div> Your ton of fun is my incredibly goofy.<br /> <br /> What is even the point? If the Lunar knows Crane Style, what are they getting out of using it in the form of a bird?<br /> <br /> Some writer comments have even suggested that there may be Lunar Charms that need to be considered against animal forms, but otherwise... yes, it's quite different.<br /> <br /> Something like a dice trick that can be applied to any kind of attack, something that neither inherently carries any assumptions of how it looks nor has much distinction from what kind of dice pool it is attached to.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:27:49-07:00","id":881171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881142#post881142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because martial arts were designed to be used by people emulating animals. Not by animals themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. A Tiger Stylist is using Martial Arts (Tiger Style) to strike you. <br /> <br /> A tiger is using Brawl.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:46:05-07:00","id":881178,"title":"","content":"I like the visuals of a Lunar in animal form fighting in quite a structured and disciplined way, and being able to do chi blocking strikes and such. Even if they are in reality chi blocking bites and slashes. Martial arts give you more than emulating an animal. I don't think a Lunar who fights as an animal should necessarily be locked into fighting with brute force.<br /> <br /> Should this be represented by using MA styles? I don't see a reason why not. But so long as it's represented, I'm fine with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:42:40-07:00","id":881234,"title":"","content":"Yeah... the general point seems to be 'MA are designed for humans to emulate animals. Not for animals to use. Which leaves me... baffled, quite honestly. At least in terms of MA charms. They use Kata's that reflect an animal and its movements. Shouldn't actually being that animal and moving like it make those charms still accessable? Why is Emulation better able to handle that?<br /> <br /> There's the question of physical strength, but that's ultimately a subissue. Lunars having the strength of their animal form or true form is a different design decision. It shouldn't affect MA though. A snake lacks a human's strength... but it's still fast, and still moves in a manner similar to a snake stylist.<br /> <br /> IDK, I'd just like to see Lunars having an incentive to fight in smaller animal forms, rather than doing the traditional thing of going straight for warform or the biggest creature they can find. It's a cool visual to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:49:20-07:00","id":881239,"title":"","content":"They can use martial arts, but it has to be Human Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Angel Toaster from Keychain of Creation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7935-cartographer7","name":"Cartographer7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7935_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:02:41-07:00","id":881248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881234#post881234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, I'd just like to see Lunars having an incentive to fight in smaller animal forms, rather than doing the traditional thing of going straight for warform or the biggest creature they can find. It's a cool visual to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to bet that there will be such incentives! In the Lunar book. Which...isn't out yet.<br /> <br /> It's so much fun to complain about the shortcomings of things that don't exist yet, though. Don't let me stop you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:03:30-07:00","id":881284,"title":"","content":"I think there at least needs to be an explanation why, in 5000 years, a bunch of shapeshifters never came up with a martial art designed to be used in animal form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:04:14-07:00","id":881286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881234#post881234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They use Kata's that reflect an animal and its movements. Shouldn't actually being that animal and moving like it make those charms still accessable? Why is Emulation better able to handle that?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSnake Style requires arms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tAir_u36C9c\u200b\" data-code=\"tAir_u36C9c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tAir_u36C9c/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-03-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:14:41-07:00","id":881293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881284#post881284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there at least needs to be an explanation why, in 5000 years, a bunch of shapeshifters never came up with a martial art designed to be used in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably have, but it probably can't be used outside of any single form or similar group of forms, so there's not much carry-over, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:32:34-07:00","id":881311,"title":"","content":"Also martial arts were developed to take a human body and push it to a limit, animals giving us something to work towards. Striking as fast as you can might be difficult to visualize, and if it's difficult to visualize it's difficult to do. Strike fast, like a snake, now there's something you can work towards. Animals don't really need to do that because usually they're already the kings of their domain. A grizzly bear has enough power to decapitate a person with a single paw swipe, a snake can strike within 1/10th of a second. There's no martial art that can improve upon that, their bodies are already performing at their absolute limit in the best possible ways.<br /> <br /> Mechanically this is represented by animals having big stats, and special innate abilities that push them even further. I mean, I guess you could be a bear, stand up on your hind legs, and try to use snake style's precision strikes and essence venom techniques, but you'd be way better off just backhanding your opponent to death in one shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:39:08-07:00","id":881313,"title":"","content":"Dude, muscles are muscles. A bear swiping at you with a claw is as close to their maximum as an untrained person slapping you with a hand is to ours.<br /> <br /> Give a bear training and they'd be able to increase their output just as much as we can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:39:52-07:00","id":881314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881284#post881284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there at least needs to be an explanation why, in 5000 years, a bunch of shapeshifters never came up with a martial art designed to be used in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple answer, complete lack of consistency among Lunars. Take a Lunar developing a snake style for a snake form. What kind of snake; poisonous or constrictor? Is the particular snake form have anything specific; partly aquatic, spits poison, senses thermal signatures, etc? All of this boils down to Joe Lunar developing his snake style that no other Lunar would feel they need. Why develop a martial art that restricts their form, when the huge advantage of a Lunar is to be able to take any form? you've essentially &quot;form-locked&quot; yourself with a highly specialized martial art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:45:05-07:00","id":881319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881234#post881234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK, I'd just like to see Lunars having an incentive to fight in smaller animal forms, rather than doing the traditional thing of going straight for warform or the biggest creature they can find. It's a cool visual to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The basic and latent abilities that ordinary animals get are pretty scary. Lunars get all basic abilities for free, and can buy latent and magical abilities, so that your &quot;wolf style&quot; isn't a literal martial arts style but rather all the powers wolves get. Given that these will likely be very cheap compared to Martial Arts, and will be able to combo freely with other Lunar charms, that seems like a good trade-off to me. Even smaller forms are likely to be able to take advantage of the Tiny Creature merit, which gives a +2 non-charm bonus to Evasion against larger enemies and has a similarly huge bonus to stealth.<br /> <br /> I expect we'll see more such abilities by the time the Lunar book is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:47:15-07:00","id":881321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881313#post881313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, muscles are muscles. A bear swiping at you with a claw is as close to their maximum as an untrained person slapping you with a hand is to ours.<br /> <br /> Give a bear training and they'd be able to increase their output just as much as we can.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given that muscular and skeletal structures are a thing and the massive variaty of them that exist, no.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, why haven't Lunars invented martial arts for animal forms? Because they don't <i>need</i> to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 05-03-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:48:16-07:00","id":881322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881284#post881284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there at least needs to be an explanation why, in 5000 years, a bunch of shapeshifters never came up with a martial art designed to be used in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would totally allow a player to come up with a dinosaur martial art that they can use while they're a dinosaur, but I would be chagrined if a dinosaur martial art actually got <i>printed.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:49:19-07:00","id":881323,"title":"","content":"Um...does anyone have a quote from someone saying this is a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:52:33-07:00","id":881326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881313#post881313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, muscles are muscles. A bear swiping at you with a claw is as close to their maximum as an untrained person slapping you with a hand is to ours.<br /> <br /> Give a bear training and they'd be able to increase their output just as much as we can.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true, except most wild animals are basically getting that training all the time. They, unlike us, live in a world where if you can't do your thing well enough, you die. A Black Mamba doesn't go through a training regimen to try and go faster and faster, pushing every last bit of speed they have out of their coiled body to snap up food because they already do that every time they want to eat. That's on top of the fact that they, unlike us, have a body that's adapted to that purpose perfectly. When a human does a snake style martial arts strike, they're learning how to coil every muscle in their body from the balls of their feet to their wrist to move at exactly the same time for maximum acceleration and power. A snake already DOES that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:58:10-07:00","id":881329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881323#post881323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...does anyone have a quote from someone saying this is a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm fairly certain there is not and it is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:01:33-07:00","id":881333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881323#post881323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...does anyone have a quote from someone saying this is a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing I recall about Lunar charm restrictions is I VAGUELY recall at one point someone saying that a Lunar can't use Evocations when they're in their Warform.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense to me, because you're in a frenzied warform.<br /> <br /> And of course, I have no idea if this is STILL true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:02:31-07:00","id":881334,"title":"","content":"I don't think its being said that animals can't improve their striking through repetition.<br /> <br /> They do, and its called Brawl. What is the difference, for a bear, of having Martial Arts (Bear Style), or Brawl? What is it trying to achieve that they are not already? What wisdom is it trying to learn, what truth, that is not already intrinsic to it, because they are already a bear?<br /> <br /> I can see an argument for a nation of sentient bears to have Roaring Bear Style or Momma Bear Style, or whatever. But just be a bear and have &quot;Bear Style&quot;? Just makes no sense to me.<br /> <br /> I believe this will be forever relegated to the realm of home brew, for its range of application is very narrow.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing is the description of Martial Arts Charms:<br /> <br /> &quot;With the exception of Excellent Solar Martial Arts, which<br /> they develop under the same conditions as other Excellencies<br /> (p. 255), the Solar Exalted don\u2019t develop native<br /> Martial Arts Charms; rather, <i>they partake of the rich tradition<br /> of martial arts techniques <b>shared between all the<br /> Exalted</b></i>. Chapter Seven presents eleven of Creation\u2019s many<br /> martial arts styles.&quot;<br /> <br /> As the IMAs will probably show, we will have some MAs that will give advantages to certain Exalts, but I think it will be a rare (if it ever appears) occurrence to see a MA that can only be practiced at all by a very narrow and specific group.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:19:56-07:00","id":881338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881323#post881323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...does anyone have a quote from someone saying this is a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* I'm the OP, and I know I'm not sure. I gave as many caveats as I could. I think it was from rpg.net a while back, but couldn't swear to it. So much has been said about Ex3 off the record, the mind can slip a bit. Sorry if I mucked this up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:27:07-07:00","id":881346,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm fairly sure this is all in the hazy undefined mysteries of the future. Don't sweat it, OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:35:21-07:00","id":881353,"title":"","content":"Can't find a direct quote, but it was referenced <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/380264-so-if-lunars-can-t-use-ma-in-animal-forms-divine-person-forms-vs-divine-beast-forms\">in this thread.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T16:49:21-07:00","id":881359,"title":"","content":"Most martial arts styles as applied to animals make no sense. The anatomy doesn't add up. A snake cannot practice Snake Style owing to having no limbs. Tigers can't use Tiger Style owing to being dedicated quadrupeds. Though bears could use Bear style; I've personally seen pandas practicing what look like staff katas. And monkeys could certainly use Monkey Style. But generally speaking, animals can't use animal styles. And they certainly can't use armed styles, what with the whole &quot;no opposable thumbs&quot; limit. Again, expect for primates and maybe pandas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T18:13:51-07:00","id":881389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881323#post881323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...does anyone have a quote from someone saying this is a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its in one of the homungeos threads in rpg.net. In one of the Ask a developer or other threads it spawned.<br /> i remember a small discusion about why being a snake would make you a good snake stylist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T18:15:40-07:00","id":881391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881326#post881326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is true, except most wild animals are basically getting that training all the time. They, unlike us, live in a world where if you can't do your thing well enough, you die. A Black Mamba doesn't go through a training regimen to try and go faster and faster, pushing every last bit of speed they have out of their coiled body to snap up food because they already do that every time they want to eat. That's on top of the fact that they, unlike us, have a body that's adapted to that purpose perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It suits the purpose pretty well, but nothing is perfect. In fact, the main operator for just about anything in nature is &quot;this is good enough&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T18:21:17-07:00","id":881393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881391#post881391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It suits the purpose pretty well, but nothing is perfect. In fact, the main operator for just about anything in nature is &quot;this is good enough&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is more like &quot;this is good enough (to outdo everything else that I have to compete with that was good enough before me)&quot;. Yes, they don't expend extra effort to become greater than they need to be, but they do need to be pretty peak condition because it is competitive. I'm not necessarily saying you're not saying that, but the way you worded it definitely conveys a different message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:07:30-07:00","id":881410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881323#post881323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um...does anyone have a quote from someone saying this is a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Demented One</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?745142-Exalted-Ask-the-Devs-pt2-(Hidden-Meaning-Behind-Veiled-Words-Style)&amp;p=18658098#post18658098\" target=\"_blank\">Tyrant Lizard special attacks + supernatural martial arts=OMGWTFBBQ</a></div> </div> </div> </div>From the same thread, a page later:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more of a &quot;that's dumb&quot; issue. Snake style may be inspired by the movements of a snake but like... you still need arms and legs to do it.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-03-2016, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:37:02-07:00","id":881422,"title":"","content":"Super happy to hear that this is up in the air. I think that any version of Exalted in which you cannot under any circumstances be a Kung Fu Panda is no version of Exalted I want to be involved in.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6lT6PgFnNWE\" data-code=\"6lT6PgFnNWE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6lT6PgFnNWE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 05-03-2016, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:43:59-07:00","id":881424,"title":"","content":"The trick is having a game where you <i>can</i> be a kung fu panda, but where &quot;Lunars as kung fu pandas&quot; does not become a fandom meme or an optimal combat build, because that would get old real fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:58:53-07:00","id":881434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881391#post881391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. It suits the purpose pretty well, but nothing is perfect. In fact, the main operator for just about anything in nature is &quot;this is good enough&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect in this case meant more &quot;Really damn good especially when compared to a human mimic.&quot; If you want to get technical nothing in the universe is perfect except maybe math. My point was more that a snake doesn't have to channel esoteric ki energy to be able to strike fast and poison his target, he's got that equipment and trained to use it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Kung Fu Panda is amazing and has way more Exalted in it than people have given it credit for, but that's totally a bunch of beastmen or DBTs, not an actual bear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-03-2016, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:26:17-07:00","id":881443,"title":"","content":"I don't think using Snake Style to attack without arms is any sillier than using Snake Style to poison people without venom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:43:42-07:00","id":881453,"title":"","content":"Regardless of official word, I will always make a rule to tie animal Martial Arts to specific Lunar totems, for a very simple reason: the Lunar charmset flat-out _cannot_ support giving 10+ Charms to the fighting style of every single animal. Even if Lunars have a Charm somewhere to fight well while prone, it will not be tied up to all the other things that make Tiger Style a very great cat-esque style in one single package. It is just a useful tool for emulation, in general, even if one says that the Charms that Lunars are using are not, actually, the same as the MA; it still allows you about 10 Charms to 'fighting like a Crane', which is very useful for someone playing a similar bird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T20:54:38-07:00","id":881460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881443#post881443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think using Snake Style to attack without arms is any sillier than using Snake Style to poison people without venom.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's designed to do the latter but not the former, is the issue. It's a specific set of techniques designed for somebody with arms! You could theoretically design a No Arms Snake Style, I guess, but it would presumably be different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:12:49-07:00","id":881472,"title":"","content":"Are you sure No Arms Snake Style would be different? Because I've got the Style open in front of me, and none of the Charms seem unfitting or silly for an actual snake.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better to say that Snake Style actually was designed to work for snakes. Can't imagine it breaking anything, or making a fight against a snake look goofy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:32:44-07:00","id":881483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881472#post881472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure No Arms Snake Style would be different? Because I've got the Style open in front of me, and none of the Charms seem unfitting or silly for an actual snake.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better to say that Snake Style actually was designed to work for snakes. Can't imagine it breaking anything, or making a fight against a snake look goofy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be pretty weird if a style designed for people with arms and a style designed for people without arms ended up being the same style just because both were designed to emulate snakes.<br /> <br /> The reason I dislike it is that the animal styles are very blatantly styles for people emulating animals. They have a lot of techniques for doing things <i>like</i> the things the animals already do, but in a way that's more appropriate for a human. It also presents the animal styles as special in a way that I don't feel they're meant to be. It's true that nothing <i>breaks</i> if you allow it (at least for now), but it strikes me as weird and out-of-theme for the styles, and I don't really see it adding much to the game.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I think we'll have to agree to disagree, since it mostly comes down to &quot;I like it better if they can&quot; versus &quot;I like it better if they can't.&quot; One day the writers will deliver us from this dilemma!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:33:25-07:00","id":881484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881472#post881472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure No Arms Snake Style would be different? Because I've got the Style open in front of me, and none of the Charms seem unfitting or silly for an actual snake.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better to say that Snake Style actually was designed to work for snakes. Can't imagine it breaking anything, or making a fight against a snake look goofy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snakes don't use hook swords or strike mystic pressure points. Their venom is entirely physical, assuming that they have it. Snake style was emphatically not made with practice by flesh and blood snakes in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T23:22:42-07:00","id":881546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881424#post881424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trick is having a game where you <i>can</i> be a kung fu panda, but where &quot;Lunars as kung fu pandas&quot; does not become a fandom meme or an optimal combat build, because that would get old real fast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Literally made the Devs watch Kung Fu Panda (one and two) with me recently. I think they said Shen was practicing Crane Style.<br /> <br /> The animal MA styles aren't about practical space and imitation, they're about psychological space and narrative heft. <br /> <br /> Totes still making a bear Lunar with epic Brawl stats and high Stamina tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T23:32:05-07:00","id":881548,"title":"","content":"I just want to get it out there that Oogway might very well be the ultimate Sidereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T02:12:33-07:00","id":881604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881422#post881422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that any version of Exalted in which you cannot under any circumstances be a Kung Fu Panda is no version of Exalted I want to be involved in.</div> </div> </div> </div> That makes me wonder; in a version of Exalted in which everybody is an anthropomorphic animal (which y'know... do that if playing anthropomorphic animals is such a big deal), what would the place of Lunars be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T02:43:32-07:00","id":881613,"title":"","content":"If I can be the weirdo who is way too intense about children's media, Po's entire martial journey is not about learning an accepted style - it is instead about accepting himself and his own body and place and strengths and weaknesses. In fact, while they're all referred to using 'styles' what it ends up being is more of a unique expression of self for each character/animal type. Po's 'style' is about his panda-ness, his size and his resilience and his faith in himself (even if he has no self-esteem through most of the first movie). He doesn't stop being fat, or a dork, or fairly slow on the uptake, or fluffy, or hopeful, or kind, or silly. He harnesses those things in order to become the best version of himself he can be, while always seeking more knowledge and experience (made much more explicit in the third movie) (which, not gonna lie, I totally got teary watching). <br /> <br /> If I were mimicking Po, I wouldn't be looking at MAs to do it - even for the harnessing of chi, I'd be going with Sorcery probably, or something like that. Or if I were, his character doesn't fit a lot of them and would mechanically be pretty weird with smatterings of everything. That said I am a straight-up Brawl fangirl so beware the bias. <br /> <br /> tl:dr - Lucy loves Po.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. ... for me, the transformative power of art is you are </span></span></span><i>not </i><span style=\"color:#5C5C5C\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">above the material.&quot; -= Guillermo del Toro</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9752-lucy-darling","name":"Lucy Darling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9752_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:05:53-07:00","id":881666,"title":"","content":"What would the kung fu panda sorcerous initiation be?<br /> <br /> Asking the real questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T07:04:49-07:00","id":881743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lucy Darling</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881613#post881613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I can be the weirdo who is way too intense about children's media</div> </div> </div> </div>My pedagogy teacher in college had us watch Kung Fu Panda in class (and that short with the training of the Furious Five was part of the discussion too), as a great example of a teacher adapting their methods to the strengths, weaknesses and needs of the student, teaching them without putting them in a mold.<br /> <br /> She is an excellent teacher, so you are in good company ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:04:21-07:00","id":881799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881666#post881666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the kung fu panda sorcerous initiation be?<br /> <br /> Asking the real questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldnt it be seeing that blank scroll and realizing that the power is inside you all along.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:10:27-07:00","id":881804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881284#post881284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there at least needs to be an explanation why, in 5000 years, a bunch of shapeshifters never came up with a martial art designed to be used in animal form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't they be better served creating a &quot;<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Kailindo\" target=\"_blank\">Kailindo</a>&quot; Martial Arts style which enhances their ability to fight like a shapeshifter who can constantly disorient their foes through assuming multiple forms of different shapes and sizes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881333#post881333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I recall about Lunar charm restrictions is I VAGUELY recall at one point someone saying that a Lunar can't use Evocations when they're in their Warform.<br /> <br /> Which makes sense to me, because you're in a frenzied warform.</div> </div> </div> </div>DBT was never frenzied, it's still not frenzied in the QC of the new corebook, and Solars can use Evocations perfectly fine even in the grips of Limit Break and the Charms called Battle-Fury Focus and Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit.<br /> <br /> Holden described the idea of DBT/Evocation exclusivity as Lunars turning so much of their magic inwards, into their bodies, that it was remarkable that they could even maintain attunement to their artifacts, which are an outward expression of power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881422#post881422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Super happy to hear that this is up in the air. I think that any version of Exalted in which you cannot under any circumstances be a Kung Fu Panda is no version of Exalted I want to be involved in.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6lT6PgFnNWE\" data-code=\"6lT6PgFnNWE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/6lT6PgFnNWE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are mostly beastfolk. Pandas cannot run on two legs like Po can, never mind WALK on two legs like Oogwei, Tai Lung, Tigress, Ox, Rhino, Gator, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:19:58-07:00","id":881813,"title":"","content":"I assume ata-beasts or various types of Wyld mutants with non-humanoid bodies could probably create and study a &quot;martial art style&quot; though it would likely be incompatible with a human's martial art style.<br /> <br /> An intelligent octopus might study and codify methods and techniques (katas) to strike harder or dodge attacks. It could be, in effect, &quot;Octo-man Style.&quot; Unfortunately, humans wouldn't be able to practice it as they lack the 8 tentacles and cartilage body required to assume the stances and use the techniques of the style. In theory a Lunar might be able to learn this style and use it while in octopus or squid form, but not other forms.<br /> <br /> Of course, this starts to get kind of silly and rather pointless really (do we really need kung-fu pandas?) so I wouldn't necessarily be adverse to it if the dev team just said that Martial Arts is for human and near human races and left it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:36:21-07:00","id":881828,"title":"","content":"At the very least ANYTHING can practice Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style as long as it has a voice or the ability to strike something loudly.<br /> <br /> But then, it WAS made by a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T08:57:35-07:00","id":881859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881828#post881828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, it WAS made by a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:01:27-07:00","id":881867,"title":"","content":"Well, it has Silver + Animal in its name.........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:09:43-07:00","id":881877,"title":"","content":"That's a bit of a stretch...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:29:53-07:00","id":881899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881859#post881859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scroll of the Monk, page 102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This weirdly musical martial art was invented late in the First Age by a Lunar Exalt with its eponymous songbird as her totem animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was the first appearance of the Style, and nothing in the Third Core contradicts it.<br /> <br /> Likewise, no one really doubts that White Reaper Style is still a Lunar invention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:30:56-07:00","id":881901,"title":"","content":"*shrug* It's a story about the First Age, so no longer firm canon. That said, yes, Silver Voiced Nightingale was originally Lunar designed. She had a domain in DotFA where everyone always sung when talking, and Scroll of the Monk had a brief bit on the style's history.<br /> <br /> (Incidently, talking of DotFA Lunar cannon... god, the Isle of Voices was the coolest idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One of very few instances when I agree with the 'less is more' philosophy of background writing.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:37:06-07:00","id":881908,"title":"","content":"Nothing contradicts it, except for the fact that as far as the new edition is concerned, Scroll of the Monk doesn't exists.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know, <i>Scroll of the Monk.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:38:34-07:00","id":881910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/881131-why-can-t-lunars-use-martial-arts-in-animal-form?p=881908#post881908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing contradicts it, except for the fact that as far as the new edition is concerned, Scroll of the Monk doesn't exists.<br /> <br /> Plus, you know, <i>Scroll of the Monk.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Not everything in Scroll of the Monk was terrible. Some of it was quite good.<br /> <br /> Case in point, <i>Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:38:57-07:00","id":881911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gra